Hi, Justin. How are the vegetables coming?

03:21.040 --> 03:24.400
Fine, Lulu. I got tomatoes and potatoes in the...

03:24.400 --> 03:27.680
When you were coming over, did you have to see a bag of beans go any other direction?

03:27.680 --> 03:29.440
Bag of beans going?

03:29.440 --> 03:31.640
You know, I always thought I understood, man.

03:31.640 --> 03:33.640
But you shake my confidence.

03:33.640 --> 03:35.640
Let's get the vegetables ready, okay?

03:35.640 --> 03:55.160
I saw that you made a snapper. Give it back! Give it back!

03:55.160 --> 03:57.800
If you're gonna afford a fur coat, you're gonna afford to pay for the vegetables.

03:57.800 --> 04:24.360
Come on down here and fix me like a man!

04:24.360 --> 04:30.040
Hey, Andy, don't feed them ponies too many apples. There ain't nothing more hungry than a pony with a bloat.

04:30.040 --> 04:32.120
Mr. Callahan, Andy, help!

04:32.120 --> 04:35.000
Terrible! Big! Out of a tree! Mouth! Teeth!

04:35.000 --> 04:38.200
And tomatoes and potatoes and...

04:38.200 --> 04:40.200
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

04:40.200 --> 04:42.760
Simmer down now! Let's try to make some sense!

04:42.760 --> 04:47.160
You're hysterical, Dusty. Now, take a deep breath and pronounce each word slowly.

04:47.160 --> 04:48.680
You ready?

04:48.680 --> 04:49.960
Begin.

04:49.960 --> 04:51.320
Tree...

04:51.320 --> 04:52.440
What about a tree?

04:52.440 --> 04:53.720
Thing...

04:53.720 --> 04:55.240
What kind of thing?

04:55.240 --> 04:56.840
Hair...

04:56.840 --> 04:59.400
Alright, you saw a hairy thing in a tree. What was it doing there?

04:59.400 --> 05:02.040
A little pointer!

05:02.040 --> 05:07.640
It had hairy arms and hairy feet and hairy toes and hairy cheeks and looked like a big, maddening wing and didn't go in again.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.440
Wait a minute! Alright, little pal. Nothing's gonna get you!

05:10.440 --> 05:12.920
Dusty, the thing you described couldn't possibly be here.

05:12.920 --> 05:13.640
It couldn't?

05:13.640 --> 05:19.000
No, the only creature answering to that description is the giant African bush gorilla and there aren't any on this continent.

05:19.000 --> 05:21.160
I wish you'd tell that the gorilla swiped my tomatoes.

05:21.160 --> 05:24.280
Now, wait a minute! There is no doubt that you saw something.

05:24.280 --> 05:29.800
But if Andy, with all his book learning, says it ain't a gorilla, that is one thing we can be sure that it ain't, huh?

05:29.800 --> 05:31.240
I didn't see a big old hairy gorilla?

05:31.240 --> 05:33.240
Absolutely not.

05:37.880 --> 05:40.760
Sure am glad I didn't see that big old hairy gorilla before.

05:40.760 --> 05:41.720
Why?

05:41.720 --> 05:51.800
Because I just didn't see him swiping those apples right now.

05:51.800 --> 05:53.080
The apples are gone!

05:53.080 --> 05:54.360
I wonder who could have taken them.

05:54.360 --> 05:57.240
Well, one thing for sure, we know it wasn't a big hairy gorilla, right Andy?

05:57.240 --> 05:57.960
Right.

05:57.960 --> 06:06.360
Well then, just get up and walk away. I mean, what in tarnation are we up against here?

06:06.360 --> 06:08.280
You hear that? Indian war drums.

06:08.280 --> 06:10.120
Those are not Indian war drums.

06:10.120 --> 06:11.320
How can you be sure of that?

06:11.320 --> 06:13.560
Because I speak drum language.

06:13.560 --> 06:21.720
And if those were Indian war drums, the message that they just sent out would be, uh...

06:21.720 --> 06:25.800
My uncle's elbow is in the house of a squirrel.

06:25.800 --> 06:27.640
Maybe the drum is a rotten speller.

06:27.640 --> 06:32.680
The one thing I know for sure, that sound is not Indian war drums.

06:32.680 --> 06:36.600
And no Indian made that footprint.

06:36.600 --> 06:38.120
What do you make of that, Andy?

06:38.120 --> 06:40.040
It's remarkable.

06:40.040 --> 06:43.560
It's the track of a simian primate in the great ape classification.

06:43.560 --> 06:45.960
Oh, thank goodness for me, I thought you were going to say gorilla.

06:45.960 --> 06:47.640
That's what he just said.

06:47.640 --> 06:52.120
I don't understand it, but I can't deny it appears to be the track of a gorilla.

06:52.120 --> 06:54.280
Deny it, deny it.

06:54.280 --> 06:58.760
I don't know what it is, but until it can be identified, we must assume it's dangerous.

06:58.760 --> 06:59.640
Yeah, very.

06:59.640 --> 07:13.960
And Harry.

07:13.960 --> 07:17.480
That thumping noise has stopped.

07:17.480 --> 07:20.120
Carter, are you sure?

07:20.120 --> 07:24.600
My dear, if I can hear interest accumulating in a vault in Boston,

07:24.600 --> 07:28.040
I can certainly hear when a noise has stopped.

07:28.040 --> 07:31.640
Listen.

07:31.640 --> 07:40.200
Yes, I distinctly hear nothing.

07:40.200 --> 07:45.000
There it isn't again.

07:45.000 --> 07:47.480
Carter, what should we do?

07:47.480 --> 07:49.560
I feel like running.

07:49.560 --> 07:51.800
Brookhavens never run.

07:51.800 --> 07:58.200
Not when they can hide.

07:58.200 --> 08:00.680
I don't know how you can be so calm, Lulu.

08:00.680 --> 08:02.680
I got a real case of the jitters.

08:02.680 --> 08:06.280
Well, when a gal earns her living doing the couch dance at the cowboy picnic,

08:06.280 --> 08:08.600
she learns not to scare so easy.

08:08.600 --> 08:10.200
Relax.

08:10.200 --> 08:13.720
I'll try, but I can't help worrying.

08:13.720 --> 08:16.680
Well, everybody gets that spooky feeling once in a while.

08:16.680 --> 08:20.520
Just keep telling yourself that you're not afraid.

08:20.520 --> 08:22.360
I'm not afraid.

08:22.360 --> 08:24.360
I'm not afraid.

08:24.360 --> 08:40.280
I'm afraid.

08:40.280 --> 08:40.840
Rusty.

08:40.840 --> 08:44.120
No!

08:44.120 --> 08:45.480
We got company.

08:45.480 --> 08:47.560
Oh, should I make some coffee and biscuits?

08:47.560 --> 08:49.800
It's not that kind of company.

08:49.800 --> 08:51.720
What do you think it is, Mr. Keller?

08:51.720 --> 08:53.720
I don't know.

08:53.720 --> 09:03.720
All right, come on out, whoever you are, and come out slow.

09:03.720 --> 09:13.720
Klaus von Schmidt, at your service.

09:13.720 --> 09:26.200
And so I have been tracking him since he's escaped.

09:26.200 --> 09:31.240
And then I see your campfire and decide I must present myself before it is too late.

09:31.240 --> 09:31.960
Yeah?

09:31.960 --> 09:32.920
What do you mean, too late?

09:34.120 --> 09:39.240
My gorilla is a ferocious and wild, wild, dangerous animal.

09:40.040 --> 09:43.400
If he hurt any of you, I should be most sorry.

09:43.400 --> 09:44.280
I knew it was a gorilla.

09:44.280 --> 09:45.560
I could smell bananas on his breath.

09:46.280 --> 09:48.840
Why don't you tell us everything you can about your gorilla?

09:48.840 --> 09:52.280
That way we stand a better chance of protecting ourselves and helping you capture him.

09:53.160 --> 09:56.280
That, Marcour, I agree with you, sir.

09:57.000 --> 10:01.880
First of all, I tell you his nomen, his name, Crank.

10:01.880 --> 10:02.440
Gesundheit.

10:03.800 --> 10:04.840
Has he escaped before?

10:06.840 --> 10:10.200
In London and in Vienna, many times.

10:10.200 --> 10:12.440
And always he does the same thing.

10:12.440 --> 10:13.240
What do you mean?

10:13.240 --> 10:15.240
First, he finds food.

10:16.120 --> 10:20.440
Then he beats his chest to establish his territory.

10:22.440 --> 10:23.240
And then?

10:23.240 --> 10:24.440
And then what?

10:24.440 --> 10:27.240
And then he steals a woman.

10:27.240 --> 10:40.760
Oh, well, at least our ladies are all safe.

10:40.760 --> 10:42.760
Oh, shit!

10:42.760 --> 10:44.760
Oh, shit!

10:44.760 --> 10:46.760
Oh, shit!

10:46.760 --> 10:48.760
Shoot, he's got Benzie!

10:48.760 --> 10:50.760
Oh, my God!

10:50.760 --> 10:52.760
Oh, my God!

10:52.760 --> 10:54.760
Stupid scum hoods, you have lost them.

10:54.760 --> 11:00.760
Now Crank has her and he will kill anyone who tries to take her back.

11:14.760 --> 11:14.760
What did you say?

11:14.760 --> 11:16.760
Well, I'm sorry, but I am excited.

11:16.760 --> 11:18.760
I forget to speak my good English.

11:18.760 --> 11:20.760
Now look, let's not lose our heads.

11:20.760 --> 11:22.760
Betsy is in trouble and she's depending upon us.

11:22.760 --> 11:26.760
Yeah, let's run after that gorilla and take Betsy away from him and give him a knuckle sandwich right in the fangs.

11:26.760 --> 11:28.760
Fine, fine.

11:30.760 --> 11:34.760
I have seen Crank tear a tree trunk in half with his bare hands.

11:36.760 --> 11:38.760
Maybe we better wait until he's tired of her.

11:38.760 --> 11:40.760
The first thing we've got to do is figure out where he's taking her.

11:40.760 --> 11:44.760
Well, if he behaves like other great apes, he's probably heading for a cave.

11:44.760 --> 11:46.760
Yeah, that is exactly right.

11:46.760 --> 11:48.760
Well, we better give up then.

11:48.760 --> 11:50.760
There's so many caves around and their mountains look like Swiss cheese.

11:50.760 --> 11:51.760
Look, we'll make search parties.

11:51.760 --> 11:53.760
You go with Klaus and you'll go with me.

11:53.760 --> 11:55.760
We'll leave Mr. Brookhaven here to look after the ladies.

11:55.760 --> 12:21.760
Come on, Andy.

12:21.760 --> 12:47.760
No, thank you. I'm not hungry.

12:47.760 --> 13:01.760
They're good.

13:01.760 --> 13:04.760
Betsy, Betsy, can you hear me?

13:04.760 --> 13:06.760
Don't you, I'm in here.

13:06.760 --> 13:10.760
Crank, it is I, Klaus, yeah?

13:10.760 --> 13:12.760
Do not harm the girl, Crank.

13:12.760 --> 13:24.760
Please, do not harm the girl.

13:24.760 --> 13:27.760
Crank may get crazy any time now.

13:27.760 --> 13:31.760
So you must hurry and find Mr. Callahan and give him an important message.

13:31.760 --> 13:33.760
Meanwhile, I shall stand watch here.

13:33.760 --> 13:37.760
Yeah, what if I go find Mr. Callahan and give him an important message while you stand watch here?

13:37.760 --> 13:39.760
That is just what I have said.

13:39.760 --> 13:46.760
I know, but it sounded so good I wanted to hear it again.

13:46.760 --> 13:49.760
So now you must take my message and do not miss a word.

13:49.760 --> 13:52.760
The exactness of the message may save the girl's life.

13:52.760 --> 13:55.760
Ja, gut? Ja, gut. Gut.

13:55.760 --> 14:02.760
Das Abersche Post ist gefügelt, der Schöne Schulische, mit der Grand Gepand, oder alles in Ordnung.

14:02.760 --> 14:05.760
Ablangen, alles in Ordnung, oder machen sie kaputt.

14:05.760 --> 14:08.760
Tot. Ja, gut? Ja, gut.

14:08.760 --> 14:14.760
Ein Mann, bitte. Young man's a message in English, is that?

14:14.760 --> 14:17.760
Och, is gone.

14:17.760 --> 14:19.760
Dummkopf.

14:19.760 --> 14:21.760
Betsy? Betsy?

14:21.760 --> 14:23.760
Betsy, where are you?

14:23.760 --> 14:24.760
Betsy?

14:24.760 --> 14:25.760
Betsy.

14:25.760 --> 14:26.760
Mr. Callahan?

14:26.760 --> 14:27.760
Hey, Dusty, is that you?

14:27.760 --> 14:28.760
Mr. Callahan?

14:28.760 --> 14:31.760
Message, quick, tell us.

14:31.760 --> 14:36.760
Ka-flungent and ka-flungent and kaput, kaput. Ja, ja, kaput, kaput. Ja, ja, ja.

14:36.760 --> 14:37.760
That's the message.

14:37.760 --> 14:40.760
Yeah, and Klaus said if I didn't get it right, then Betsy might get hurt real bad.

14:40.760 --> 14:42.760
Well, obviously Klaus remained behind to guard something.

14:42.760 --> 14:46.760
Right, we found the cave where Gronk took Betsy, and Klaus, you know, said I gotta find you guys,

14:46.760 --> 14:47.760
well, he stayed behind and was lookout.

14:47.760 --> 14:49.760
That's what the message must have said.

14:49.760 --> 14:51.760
How about that, I can speak German.

14:51.760 --> 14:52.760
Let's make tracks.

14:52.760 --> 14:53.760
Not yet.

14:53.760 --> 14:55.760
Now, without a plan, we run the risk of irritating Gronk with no purpose.

14:55.760 --> 15:02.760
Yeah, we gotta have a plan.

15:02.760 --> 15:04.760
Has anybody seen Annie's equipment chest?

15:04.760 --> 15:05.760
It's over there on the wagon.

15:05.760 --> 15:07.760
Yeah, I gotta get some stuff to take care of Gronk.

15:07.760 --> 15:10.760
Oh, I didn't know Annie had a cannon in there.

15:10.760 --> 15:14.760
It's not a gun, it's some kind of scientific formula in a big bottle.

15:14.760 --> 15:15.760
That's not it.

15:15.760 --> 15:19.760
If you can tell us what it is you're seeking, perhaps we can help you seek.

15:19.760 --> 15:23.760
I can't remember the name, but it sounds kind of funny.

15:23.760 --> 15:27.760
Potassium cyanide.

15:27.760 --> 15:31.760
Ah, fulminate of mercury.

15:31.760 --> 15:34.760
This is it.

15:34.760 --> 15:42.760
Chloroform.

15:42.760 --> 15:44.760
All right, now let's go over the plan one more time, Dusty.

15:44.760 --> 15:48.760
Klaus and I will rig the net over the mouth of the cave just out of Gronk's sight.

15:48.760 --> 15:51.760
Right, I make a noise outside so he comes outside to see it.

15:51.760 --> 15:53.760
Yeah, and then you and Klaus drop the net over him,

15:53.760 --> 15:56.760
and I'll get in there and wrestle with him until you can get the chloroform in his mouth.

15:56.760 --> 15:58.760
Yeah, but you must do it quickly.

15:58.760 --> 16:00.760
You better believe it, I can't wrestle that ape too long.

16:00.760 --> 16:01.760
Don't you worry.

16:01.760 --> 16:06.760
As soon as he steps out, I'll just give it to him right in the mouth and just kind of hold it there until he gets on face and...

16:06.760 --> 16:07.760
Boy, he's touch me strong.

16:07.760 --> 16:09.760
And then I just hold on to it.

16:22.760 --> 16:26.760
Now listen, you start to make ruckus as soon as I give the signal and hurry with that stuff

16:26.760 --> 16:28.760
because I can't wrestle that gorilla for very long.

16:28.760 --> 16:31.760
Right.

16:31.760 --> 16:50.760
Grom, hey Grom, hey Grom, come out of here.

16:50.760 --> 17:02.760
Grom is a sissy, Grom is a sissy.

17:02.760 --> 17:30.760
Grom, hey, come on, get him, get him, get him, get him.

17:30.760 --> 17:34.760
Anybody ever make some boxing gloves big enough to fit long fingernails,

17:34.760 --> 17:36.760
there's going to be a new heavyweight champ of the world.

17:36.760 --> 17:38.760
In fact, Grom sure was angry when he got back to his cave.

17:38.760 --> 17:43.760
I mean, there was steam coming out of his eyes.

17:43.760 --> 17:45.760
I bet she's still in trouble.

17:45.760 --> 17:46.760
Nothing to do but go try again.

17:46.760 --> 17:48.760
No, I ain't, I ain't.

17:48.760 --> 17:52.760
Grom could be twice as suspicious as before and even more deadly.

17:52.760 --> 17:54.760
I still say that chloroform is the answer.

17:54.760 --> 17:56.760
The problem is getting him to take it.

17:56.760 --> 17:58.760
Why don't we give him a ham and chloroform sandwich?

17:58.760 --> 18:00.760
That's ridiculous.

18:00.760 --> 18:02.760
The only food that Grom loves is bananas.

18:02.760 --> 18:05.760
Are you suggesting that we give him a chloroform banana?

18:05.760 --> 18:07.760
That's it.

18:07.760 --> 18:09.760
The problem is getting him to take it.

18:09.760 --> 18:12.760
If only we were in Dusseldorf.

18:12.760 --> 18:14.760
What, what do you, in Dussel whatever, what did you say?

18:14.760 --> 18:15.760
What is that?

18:15.760 --> 18:19.760
Because there's a little chimpanzee in the zoo there who is best friends with Grom.

18:19.760 --> 18:23.760
For some reason Grom is always very gentle with monkeys.

18:23.760 --> 18:26.760
You mean if we had a little gorilla we could get him to take a loaded banana?

18:26.760 --> 18:29.760
Wait, you gotta find a little gorilla in this...

18:35.760 --> 18:37.760
Well, it may not be perfect but it's a rush job.

18:37.760 --> 18:38.760
Hmph.

18:38.760 --> 18:40.760
That is great.

18:40.760 --> 18:41.760
I can't go through life like this.

18:41.760 --> 18:44.760
But Dusty, Mrs. Brookhaven's percol looks just fine.

18:50.760 --> 18:53.760
Just get him to trust you and you give him that, huh?

18:53.760 --> 18:54.760
Don't worry Mr. Callahan.

18:54.760 --> 18:56.760
I'll have the gorilla eating out of my arm.

18:56.760 --> 18:57.760
I mean my hand.

18:57.760 --> 18:59.760
I mean my rule. I wish I hadn't said that.

18:59.760 --> 19:02.760
Just get him out in the open and I'll finish him off with this buffoon gun.

19:02.760 --> 19:04.760
Nein, nein, you must not do this.

19:04.760 --> 19:06.760
Grom is an extremely rare specimen.

19:06.760 --> 19:08.760
You must appeal to his gentleness.

19:08.760 --> 19:11.760
Then he will trust you and he will take the banana.

19:11.760 --> 19:15.760
Okay, but this is the last time I let anybody make a monkey out of me.

19:15.760 --> 19:20.760
All right, there goes a brave little guy.

19:39.760 --> 19:40.760
I'm not angry this time.

19:40.760 --> 19:42.760
I think you've got an interesting...

19:42.760 --> 19:45.760
Betsy, when you get out run to me.

19:45.760 --> 19:46.760
Turn right.

20:02.760 --> 20:03.760
That's it!

20:03.760 --> 20:05.760
You're doing fine.

20:05.760 --> 20:06.760
That's it.

20:35.760 --> 20:38.760
Give me a hand. Give me a hand.

20:38.760 --> 20:39.760
Right.

20:45.760 --> 20:46.760
Get my knee under.

20:46.760 --> 20:49.760
We'll get you out there in a minute, Betsy.

20:49.760 --> 20:52.760
Sorry Grom, I can't play anymore.

20:58.760 --> 20:59.760
Keep it up.

20:59.760 --> 21:01.760
You got to finish him.

21:01.760 --> 21:05.760
Help, somebody help.

21:05.760 --> 21:07.760
Don't show fear.

21:07.760 --> 21:09.760
I'm going to make you panic.

21:11.760 --> 21:13.760
You're embracing Grom does.

21:13.760 --> 21:15.760
That's how apes show friendship.

21:15.760 --> 21:17.760
Do what he does.

21:19.760 --> 21:20.760
Come on, Betsy.

21:20.760 --> 21:21.760
You take care of Betsy.

21:21.760 --> 21:23.760
I'm going to help, bless you.

21:23.760 --> 21:25.760
He's getting mad with you.

21:25.760 --> 21:27.760
Give him some banana.

21:27.760 --> 21:29.760
Give him some banana.

21:34.760 --> 21:36.760
No thanks, I've already had enough.

21:36.760 --> 21:38.760
I really don't want it.

21:38.760 --> 21:39.760
I just don't want it.

21:39.760 --> 21:40.760
No, you can have it.

21:40.760 --> 21:41.760
I don't want it anymore, really.

21:41.760 --> 21:42.760
Just give me enough.

21:42.760 --> 21:44.760
Don't worry, I don't want any of it.

21:45.760 --> 21:47.760
How's he doing?

21:48.760 --> 21:49.760
You see?

21:49.760 --> 21:51.760
Monkey do, monkey see.

21:52.760 --> 21:53.760
You see?

21:53.760 --> 21:54.760
You see?

21:54.760 --> 21:57.760
Monkey do, monkey see.

22:14.760 --> 22:15.760
You did it.

22:15.760 --> 22:16.760
You knocked him out.

22:16.760 --> 22:17.760
How?

22:17.760 --> 22:18.760
You ate some banana too.

22:18.760 --> 22:20.760
I only pretended to eat it so we would do what I did.

22:20.760 --> 22:24.760
You thought I took a bite like this.

22:40.760 --> 22:45.760
Well, little pal, I certainly am glad that Kraus and Kronk got themselves back to that circus.

22:45.760 --> 22:48.760
Yeah, I don't have to worry about wild African animals bothering us anymore.

22:48.760 --> 22:51.760
No, that couldn't happen again in a month or Sundays.

22:58.760 --> 23:00.760
You think lions like bananas?

23:00.760 --> 23:17.760
Wagons, go!

